    "summary": "Man&#039;s wrapper (Ewe kente); composed of twenty-four narrow strips, hand sewn together. Repeating warp stripes in green, red, white and indigo. Supplementary weft float patterns and weft-faced pattern bands in multi-coloured cotton (predominantly purple and yellow). Aligned weft-faced blocks in stripes of purple and yellow cotton at both ends of wrapper. Loose warp thread fringes at both ends.",
